  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young Mayan women strengthening democracy in Huehuetenango</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Red Maya, Cimujer (REDMAYA), a grassroots organization comprised of 32 young indigenous women leaders from Guatemala&apos;s Huehuetenango, will learn about management and fundraising, as well as topics related to citizenship and democracy, and social audits, a practice that allows Guatemalan citizens to use existing laws and regulations to ensure that development initiatives are implemented following due process. In doing so, REDMAYA will strengthen its relationships with civil society and local governments to promote the rights of women and youth and the reestablishing of a municipal office on women. Grant activities will benefit 450 people directly and some 10,000 indirectly.</narrative>
  </description>
